# The corpus IS committed, reversing the rule that used to stand here — with
# one exception, corpus/works/, excluded below. The copyright position, and
# what a takedown costs now that the texts are in git history rather than only
# in a build, are stated in corpus/README.md; the reasoning is in
# docs/decisions.md.

# Corpus: parsed output only. corpus/raw/ stays tracked — it is the only
# artifact that cost requests against someone else's server, and a re-crawl is
# the sole way back to it. corpus/works/ is a pure function of raw/ plus
# pipeline/, verified byte-for-byte reproducible offline in under three
# minutes; see corpus/README.md for how to rebuild it.
/corpus/works/

# Python
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Node / SvelteKit
node_modules/
site/.svelte-kit/
site/build/

# Empty dotfiles recreated by Claude Code's sandbox shell init — not project files
.bash_profile
.bashrc
.gitconfig
.gitmodules
.profile
.ripgreprc
.zprofile
.zshrc

# Editor / tooling state, not project files. No trailing slashes: the
# sandbox shell init recreates .idea/.vscode as empty *files*, not dirs.
.claude
.idea
.vscode
.mcp.json

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log
